WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.484
FedRAMP evidence and documentation connect security claims to real system implementation, operations, assessment, monitoring, findings, remediation, and risk decisions.

2
00:00:11.484 --> 00:00:26.183
They help stakeholders understand what the cloud service offering is, how controls are implemented, what evidence supports those controls, what weaknesses remain, and whether security posture is being maintained over time.

3
00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:34.911
Strong documentation is scoped, consistent, current, specific, evidence-backed, and aligned to the actual cloud service offering.

4
00:00:34.911 --> 00:00:44.175
It describes the real boundary, dependencies, shared responsibilities, control implementations, procedures, and operational processes.

5
00:00:44.175 --> 00:00:51.678
It avoids generic promises, unsupported statements, and idealized descriptions that do not match the live system.

6
00:00:51.678 --> 00:00:54.587
Consistency across documents is essential.

7
00:00:54.587 --> 00:01:04.004
Strong evidence is traceable, relevant, reviewable, protected, and connected to control assertions, findings, remediation, and monitoring.

8
00:01:04.004 --> 00:01:07.373
It has an owner, context, date, source, and purpose.

9
00:01:07.373 --> 00:01:12.426
It supports a specific claim rather than floating as an unexplained artifact.

10
00:01:12.426 --> 00:01:20.771
It is managed carefully because it may contain sensitive security, architecture, vulnerability, or operational information.

11
00:01:20.771 --> 00:01:23.221
The goal is not documentation volume.

12
00:01:23.221 --> 00:01:27.049
More documents do not automatically mean better security.

13
00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:35.623
The goal is trustworthy evidence that helps stakeholders understand whether controls are implemented and operating as described.

14
00:01:35.623 --> 00:01:50.935
When evidence and documentation are accurate, current, and connected to action, they become practical decision support for assessment, authorization support, continuous monitoring, customer reuse, and risk-informed operations.
